= Concentrated liquidity — Simple =

Concentrated liquidity lets a liquidity provider choose a price range where their capital is active. This can make capital more useful near the current price, but the position stops earning swap fees from that pool when price moves outside its active range.

'''Important boundary:''' concentrated liquidity ≠ Uniswap by identity.

